# Rank 1598 / CVE-2024-9710: PostHog's external data source creation
# passed the request's subdomain into its credential validation and
# outbound URL construction without any character check, so a crafted
# subdomain redirected the server's own connections (host segment
# injection toward SSRF, CWE-20/CWE-918; PR #25388). The Zendesk and
# Vitally branches of ExternalDataSourceViewSet in
# posthog/warehouse/api/external_data_source.py did `subdomain =
# request.data.get("subdomain", "")` then straight into
# validate_zendesk_credentials(subdomain=subdomain, ...) -- the
# helper builds https://{subdomain}.zendesk.com/... and the segment
# accepts slashes, dots and query characters. Pool commit 3732c0fd95
# is the real fix (COMMIT_OK -- "fix(data-warehouse): Check source
# subdomains are correct (#25388)"): both branches compile
# `^[a-zA-Z-]+$` and reject with 400 before any validation or URL
# construction. No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, host-segment validation at project boundaries. The
# subdomain crosses from request.data into PostHog's own credential
# helper whose URL construction is invisible to the scanner -- the
# project-API boundary of ranks 1545/1579 -- and the corpus's
# request-data sources label the input while no sink labels the
# helper's outbound call, so no taint path forms (scanning the file
# reports the same findings at both revisions; none on the subdomain
# flow). The fix's control -- a character-class allowlist on the
# host segment -- is the general shape. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1598 records the raw
# subdomain reaching the credential helper and the regex-gated form,
# both asserting reject VYQL-RF-001: when helper-boundary vocabulary
# lands, the raw form must flip to expect.

test "rank1598: the subdomain reaches the helper unchecked"
  lang python
  file posthog/warehouse/api/external_data_source.py
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  from rest_framework import request, status
  from rest_framework.response import Response


  class ExternalDataSourceViewSet(viewsets.ModelViewSet):
      def create(self, request):
          if source_type == "Zendesk":
              subdomain = request.data.get("subdomain", "")
              api_key = request.data.get("api_key", "")
              email_address = request.data.get("email_address", "")

              if not validate_zendesk_credentials(
                  subdomain=subdomain, api_key=api_key, email_address=email_address
              ):
                  return Response(
                      status=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST,
                      data={"message": "Invalid credentials: Zendesk credentials are incorrect"},
                  )

          return Response(status=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)
  ```

test "rank1598: the fix allowlists the subdomain characters"
  lang python
  file posthog/warehouse/api/external_data_source.py
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  import re

  from rest_framework import request, status
  from rest_framework.response import Response


  class ExternalDataSourceViewSet(viewsets.ModelViewSet):
      def create(self, request):
          if source_type == "Zendesk":
              subdomain = request.data.get("subdomain", "")
              api_key = request.data.get("api_key", "")
              email_address = request.data.get("email_address", "")

              subdomain_regex = re.compile("^[a-zA-Z-]+$")
              if not subdomain_regex.match(subdomain):
                  return Response(
                      status=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST,
                      data={"message": "Invalid credentials: Zendesk subdomain is incorrect"},
                  )

              if not validate_zendesk_credentials(
                  subdomain=subdomain, api_key=api_key, email_address=email_address
              ):
                  return Response(
                      status=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST,
                      data={"message": "Invalid credentials: Zendesk credentials are incorrect"},
                  )

          return Response(status=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)
  ```
